.TH OPENWITTY-CLI 1 "November 2026" "openwitty 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openwitty-cli \- diagnostic tool for the LEWITT CONNECT 2 (unofficial, experimental)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openwitty-cli
.RB { devices | diagnose | list | probe " [" \-\-execute "] | read"
.IR what " [" options "] | write"
.IR field " " value " [" options "] | \-\-version }"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B openwitty-cli
inspects LEWITT USB devices (vendor id 0x29c2) and performs single control transfers. It is
read-only by default; four experimental write commands each change exactly one setting and
need explicit opt-in. This software is not affiliated with LEWITT.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B devices
List LEWITT devices from sysfs: descriptors, interfaces, bound kernel drivers and node
permissions. No USB traffic is sent.
.TP
.B diagnose
Like \fBdevices\fR, with an explanation of what each finding means for control access.
.TP
.B list
Quick libusb enumeration (vendor/product id only).
.TP
.BR probe " [" \-\-execute ]
Dry run (default) or execution of a small matrix of GET-only experiments.
.TP
.BR read " " api | version | status | settings
Read one message. Options:
.BR \-\-mock " (simulated device), " \-\-interface " N|auto, " \-\-method " interface|device-recipient|detach,"
.BR \-\-request " uac2|uac1."
.TP
.BR write " " led-brightness " 0-100 | " instrument-mute " on|off | " speaker-volume " -60..0 | " speaker-mute " on|off"
Change one setting. Without \fB\-\-execute\fR only a dry-run proposal is printed and nothing is
sent. With \fB\-\-execute\fR on real hardware: a fresh settings snapshot, one SET limited to the
bytes of that setting, read-back verification, never retried.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 3 permission denied (EACCES); 4 interface busy (EBUSY); 5 stall (EPIPE); 6 timeout;
7 device absent; 8 unsupported; 9 bad response; 64 usage error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LEWITT_ALLOW_HARDWARE_WRITE
Must be exactly \fB1\fR for any \fBwrite \-\-execute\fR on real hardware.
.TP
.BR LEWITT_ALLOW_WRITE_INSTRUMENT_MUTE ", " LEWITT_ALLOW_WRITE_SPEAKER_VOLUME
Additionally required (exactly \fB1\fR) for instrument-mute, resp. speaker-volume and speaker-mute.
.TP
.B LEWITT_ALLOW_DISRUPTIVE
Must be set, in addition to \fB\-\-method detach\fR, to allow detaching the kernel audio driver
(this removes the sound card while it runs). Never set by default.
.SH NOTES
Only one OpenWitty process uses the device at a time. While
.BR openwitty (1)
or
.BR openwitty-volumed (1)
holds it, device commands report that the control is in use.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openwitty (1),
.BR openwitty-volumed (1),
/usr/share/doc/openwitty/USB_PERMISSIONS.md
